.TH BUP 1 "2026-03-27" "bup" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bup \- create compressed tarball backups of directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bup
.IR directory ...
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bup
creates compressed tarball backups of one or more directories with
automatic conflict-free naming, optional encryption, retention
management, and pre/post script execution.
.PP
Tarballs are named
.BR bak. \fIdirname\fR . \fIYYYY-mm-dd\fR .tgz
and a numeric suffix is appended if a file with the same name already
exists.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output_directory"
Write the tarball to
.I output_directory
instead of the current directory.
.TP
.BI \-x " pattern" "\fR,\fP \-\-exclude " pattern
Exclude files matching
.IR pattern .
Can be specified multiple times.
Patterns are passed to
.BR tar (1)'s
.B \-\-exclude
option.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-vcs
Exclude version control system files (.git, .svn, etc.).
Passed to
.BR tar (1)
as
.BR \-\-exclude\-vcs .
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-artifacts
Exclude common build outputs, dependency directories, caches, and IDE
files.
See
.B EXCLUSION PATTERNS
below.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-secrets
Exclude common secrets, credentials, private keys, and environment
files.
See
.B EXCLUSION PATTERNS
below.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-dev
Shorthand for
.B \-\-exclude\-artifacts \-\-exclude\-secrets\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-excludes
Print the full list of artifact and secret exclusion patterns and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
Sets the
.B BUP_VERBOSE
environment variable to
.B 1
for pre/post scripts and passes
.B v
to
.BR tar (1).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would happen without creating a backup or modifying any files.
.TP
.B \-\-combined
When multiple directories are given, bundle them into a single tarball
instead of creating one tarball per directory.
The tarball is named
.BR bak. \fIdir1\fR + \fIdir2\fR . \fIdate\fR .tgz .
.TP
.BI \-z " algo" "\fR,\fP \-\-compress " algo
Choose the compression algorithm.
.I algo
must be one of
.BR gzip " (default), " bzip2 ", " xz ", or " zstd .
The file extension is set accordingly:
.BR .tgz ", " .tbz2 ", " .txz ", " .tzst .
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-encrypt
Encrypt the tarball with
.BR gpg (1)
using symmetric encryption.
The user is prompted for a passphrase.
The output file has a
.B .gpg
suffix appended (e.g.,
.BR .tgz.gpg ).
.TP
.BI \-\-recipient " KEY"
Encrypt using asymmetric GPG encryption with
.IR KEY .
Implies
.BR \-e .
.TP
.BI \-\-keep " N"
After creating the backup, keep only the
.I N
most recent backups for the same directory in the output directory and
delete the rest.
.TP
.BI \-\-prune " N"
Standalone mode: delete old backups, keeping only the
.I N
most recent.
No new backup is created.
Requires at least one directory argument to identify which backups to
prune.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List existing backups in the output directory in a table showing date,
size, and filename.
If directories are specified, only backups for those directories are
shown.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list\-verbose
Like
.B \-\-list
but also shows the file count inside each tarball.
Encrypted tarballs display
.B (encrypted)
instead.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-save\-script
Generate an executable shell script that re-runs
.B bup
with the same arguments (excluding script-generation flags).
Defaults to
.B ./backup.sh\fR.
.TP
.BI \-S " name" "\fR,\fP \-\-script\-name " name
Use
.I name
instead of
.BR backup.sh .
Implies
.BR \-s .
.TP
.BI \-d " directory" "\fR,\fP \-\-script\-dir " directory
Write the generated script to
.I directory
instead of the current directory.
Implies
.BR \-s .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show built-in help and exit.
.SH EXCLUSION PATTERNS
.SS Artifact patterns (\-\-exclude\-artifacts)
.B Dependency directories:
node_modules, bower_components, vendor, .bundle, jspm_packages, packages
.PP
.B Build outputs:
target, build, dist, out, bin, obj, _build, cmake-build-*, *.egg-info,
__pycache__, *.pyc
.PP
.B Caches:
\&.cache, .parcel-cache, .next, .nuxt, .turbo, .angular, .svelte-kit,
\&.gradle, .sass-cache, .pytest_cache, .mypy_cache, .ruff_cache, .tox,
\&.nox, .venv, venv, .eggs, .hypothesis, .coverage, htmlcov,
\&.phpunit.cache, .jest-cache
.PP
.B IDE / editor:
\&.idea, .vs, .vscode, *.swp, *.swo, *~, .DS_Store
.PP
.B Misc:
artifacts, .terraform, .serverless, cdk.out, .aws-sam, .vagrant
.SS Secret patterns (\-\-exclude\-secrets)
.B Environment files:
\&.env, .env.*, appsettings.json, appsettings.*.json, secrets.json,
local.settings.json
.PP
.B Credentials / keys:
*.pem, *.key, *.p12, *.pfx, *.jks, *.keystore, credentials.json,
service-account*.json, *.gpg-key, .npmrc, .pypirc, .docker/config.json,
\&.netrc, .htpasswd
.PP
.B Cloud / infrastructure:
terraform.tfvars, *.tfvars, .aws/credentials
.PP
.B SSH keys:
id_rsa, id_ed25519, id_ecdsa
.SH AUTOMATIC SCRIPT EXECUTION
If a file named
.B .bup\-pre.sh
exists in the target directory, it is executed before the backup.
If the script fails (non-zero exit), the backup is aborted.
.PP
If a file named
.B .bup\-post.sh
exists in the target directory, it is executed after the backup.
If the script fails, a warning is issued but the backup is retained.
.PP
Both scripts run with the target directory as the working directory and
receive
.B BUP_VERBOSE=1
when verbose mode is enabled.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BUP_VERBOSE
Set to
.B 1
when
.B \-\-verbose
is used.
Available to .bup\-pre.sh and .bup\-post.sh scripts.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to any value to disable colored output.
See
.UR https://no-color.org
.UE .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (invalid arguments, directory not found, tar failure,
pre-script failure, etc.).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bup /home/user/project
bup /home/user/project \-o /backup
bup /home/user/project \-\-verbose
bup /home/user/project \-x "*.log" \-x "*.tmp"
bup /home/user/project \-\-exclude\-dev
bup /home/user/projA /home/user/projB \-o /backup
bup /home/user/projA /home/user/projB \-\-combined
bup /home/user/project \-z xz \-e \-\-keep 5
bup /home/user/project \-\-prune 3 \-o /backup
bup \-\-list \-o /backup
bup /home/user/project \-L \-o /backup
bup /home/user/project \-s \-o /backup
bup \-\-show\-excludes
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tar (1),
.BR gpg (1),
.BR test\-bup (1)
